# Settings for permits_api.py
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Make a copy named .env in the same folder:   cp .env_template .env
#   2. Replace the example values below with your own.
#   3. Never commit .env to git (it's listed in .gitignore).

# ID of the Google Cloud project that owns the bucket.
# Find it in the Google Cloud console: click the project picker at the top; it's in the "ID" column.
# Our team's project: houseprice-510122
GCP_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id

# Name of the Cloud Storage bucket where the collected data is saved.
# Find it in the console under Cloud Storage -> Buckets.
# Our team's bucket: house_prices_bucket
GCS_BUCKET_NAME=your-bucket-name

# Optional: path to a service account key file (JSON).
# Leave this commented out if you logged in with:  gcloud auth application-default login
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/your-key.json
